  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 132 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nThursday through Friday...Ensemble and upper jet trends suggest \nthat the local area to benefit from becoming under the influence of \nsome of the ridging of the blocked pattern aloft, which would \nlead to some fine fair weather fall days with highs in the 60s \nto near 70 and overnight lows in the 50s and 40s. Will have to \nwatch for some upper trof energy to try and undercut the ridging\nand shuttle some showers or way Thu or into Friday, but the \nlatest ensembles suggest an omega ridge to get pumped up along \nthe MS RVR Valley from subsidence off developing east coast deep\ncyclone and erode precip as it tries to near the area from the \nwest Thursday and especially on Friday.\n\nSaturday and Sunday...Getting into a more uncertain period, but the \nsame ensembles suggest another ridge-undercutting trof may finally \nbring in some shower chances to the area Sat into early Sunday. \nCurrently temps look seasonable for the weekend.",
